## Consolidated Source Registry (auto-generated from tool calls)
Use ONLY these sources when writing the final report. Each has been verified as a real tool result and annotated with a source class. You may use these [N] numbers directly or assign your own — citations will be auto-verified and renumbered.

For broad standard reports, cite a representative spread of the strongest sources across all major sections. Do not collapse the evidence base to only a few references when many relevant verified sources are available.

Match source class to claim class: use `first_party` for named-entity specifications, pricing, limits, API behavior, release notes, and feature support; use `primary_issuer` for statistics/data; use `academic` for empirical or causal claims; use `authoritative_third_party` and `trade_press` for independent synthesis; use `content_marketing`, `vendor_marketing`, and `forum` sources only with visible calibration.

