Source class definitions:
- `first_party`: official documentation, help center, API reference, or release notes from the named entity's owner
- `primary_issuer`: original publisher of data/statistics, government reports, statutes, analyst reports, or official datasets
- `academic`: peer-reviewed papers, preprints, conference proceedings, or scholarly indexes
- `authoritative_third_party`: established API marketplaces, model registries, repositories, reference works, or reputable technical publications
- `trade_press`: industry journalism or professional publications with editorial standards
- `vendor_marketing`: vendor landing pages, pricing pages, case studies, and product marketing pages
- `content_marketing`: tutorial, SEO, commentary, or aggregator pages
- `forum`: Reddit, Stack Overflow, Hacker News, or community discussion
- `unknown`: source class could not be determined
